  "summary": "Phase 6.2: clip tagging UI — ClipTagScreen with cue-select, scrub bar, ±1 frame buttons, in-place Dexie update. New module `app/src/clipmode/tag.ts` exports `FRAME_STEP_MS = 1000/30`, `stepFrame(currentMs, delta, durationMs)`, and `clampCueAtMs(cueAtMs, durationMs)` as pure helpers (11 tests). Library gains `getClip(id)` and `updateClipTag(id, { cueId, cueAtMs })` — clamps cueAtMs to [0, durationMs] and overwrites in place (5 new tests, 28 total in library.test.ts; was 23). New `app/src/ui/ClipTagScreen.tsx` (chunk: 3.08 KB / 1.22 KB gzip, lazy-loaded via React.lazy matching the PairScreen / ClipLibraryScreen idiom) renders <video controls> on a blob URL, a range-input scrub bar bound to cueAtMs, ±1 frame buttons, an 8-option cue-type select sourced from `CUE_LIBRARY`, and a Save button that persists via `updateClipTag` and shows a saved-indicator. Prefills cueId + cueAtMs from the existing clip record if a prior tag exists. N
