[tool_use] Agent {"description":"Code review Phase 6.3","subagent_type":"code-reviewer","prompt":"Review the Phase 6.3 implementation in the pointfight-reactor repository (working tree against HEAD = 1ca0b8c \"phase-6.2: clip tagging UI\").\n\nPhase 6.3 ships the final phase of the project: clip-mode drill + RT measurement + per-clip results. It is the project-complete signal phase per `artifacts/decision-memo.md` §\"Project-complete signal\".\n\nAcceptance criteria from `docs/PHASES.md` §\"Phase 6.3\":\n1. New pure module `engine/persistence.ts` exposes `commitRep(...)` containing the invariants currently inlined in `src/store/session.ts:107-139` (rep-id minting, resolveCueAtDistance, roundIndex + inputSource fan-out, persistSession(null) boundary, feedback hand-off). Both `session.ts` and `clipmode/runner.ts` call it.\n2. `RepRecord` gains `clipId?: string`. `SessionRecord` gains `mode?: 'live' | 'clip'` (undefined ≡ 'live' for back-compat).\n3. `clipmode/runner.ts` selects clips by uniform random with replacement, no repeat-immediately-previous. Untagged clips excluded. Distribution test: 200 draws from 5 clips, each 32-48 times. No-repeat-prev test: 100 draws from ≥2 clips, no consecutive duplicates.\n4. IdleScreen segmented control `data-testid='mode-segmented'` with `mode-live` + `mode-clip`. Default live. Start dispatches based on mode; no second Start button. Clip-mode Start inherits phone-pairing gate.\n5. `clipmode/runtime.ts:isClipModeSupported()` returns false when `requestVideoFrameCallback` is absent. IdleScreen renders `data-testid='clip-mode-unsupported'` banner and disables Start.\n6. Clip mode with zero tagged clips disables Start with `data-testid='clip-mode-no-clips'` banner.\n7. `ClipDrillScreen.tsx` mounts `<video>`, drives the runner, renders same feedback UI as TrainerScreen. `cueShownAt = clipStartedAt + clip.cueAtMs` via requestVideoFrameCallback callback timestamp.\n8. Saved `SessionRecord.mode === 'clip'`; each `RepRecord` has correct `clipId`. Phase-5 analytics unchanged.\n9. SummaryScreen shows per-clip breakdown when mode === 'clip', using `cueBreakdown(reps)` filtered by clipId.\n10. Lint + tsc + vitest + vite build clean. Bundle budget: +6 KB gzip.\n11. Manual real-device QA at `app/verify-phase6-3.mjs`. ±33 ms cue-shown precision is MANUAL per §B5.\n12. The 6.3 phase-approval.json sets `\"project_complete\": true`; next iteration writes `artifacts/project-complete.json` with `final_phase: \"6.3\"`, `deferred: [\"phase-7\"]`.\n\nFiles (new or modified):\n- `app/src/engine/persistence.ts` — NEW. Synchronous `commitRep(input): CommitRepResult` that builds the RepRecord, fires `void saveRep(rep)` as a side-effect, returns `{ rep, feedback, effective }`. Sync to preserve the live drill's synchronous press→feedback transition since Phase 1.\n- `app/src/engine/persistence.test.ts` — NEW 7 tests covering full rep shape, persistence round-trip, distance omission, distance writing, clipId writing, clipId omission, id uniqueness.\n- `app/src/engine/types.ts` — added `clipId?: string` to RepRecord; `mode?: 'live' | 'clip'` to SessionRecord.\n- `app/src/store/session.ts` — refactored `commitRep` closure to call into `engine/persistence.commitRep`. No behavioral change; existing 17 session tests still pass.\n- `app/src/clipmode/runtime.ts` — NEW. `isClipModeSupported()` feature-detects HTMLVideoElement.prototype.requestVideoFrameCallback. Exports `CLIP_MODE_UNSUPPORTED_MESSAGE`.\n- `app/src/clipmode/runtime.test.ts` — NEW 2 tests stubbing the prototype.\n- `app/src/clipmode/random.ts` — NEW. `pickNextClip(rng, clipIds, previousId)` — uniform random with no immediate repeat. Edge-cases: empty (throws), single-clip (returns it), prev-not-in-list (uniform fallback).\n- `app/src/clipmode/random.test.ts` — NEW 6 tests including 200-draw distribution + 100-draw no-repeat-prev. Distribution test uses mulberry32(1) seed to land each clip in 32–48 range.\n- `app/src/clipmode/runner.ts` — NEW Zustand slice. State machine: idle → precue → showing → feedback → ended. `start()` filters to tagged clips, picks initial. `markClipStarted` / `markCueShown` from rvfc callbacks. `recordPress` routes through `commitRep` with `clipId`. `acknowledgeFeedback` picks next clip. `stop()` persists SessionRecord with `mode: 'clip'`.\n- `app/src/clipmode/runner.test.ts` — NEW 12 tests: empty-pool no-op, start initializes, mark+mark advances phase, correct_go with clipId, pre-cue false_start with clipId, finishWindow late with clipId, acknowledge selects next no-repeat, maxReps ends with mode='clip' persisted, stop persists with endedAt + mode='clip', phone inputSource carried.\n- `app/src/ui/ClipDrillScreen.tsx` — NEW. Mounts `<video>`, blob URL effect, rvfc loop watching `metadata.mediaTime * 1000 >= clip.cueAtMs` then calls `markCueShown(performance.now())`. Keyboard + phone-peer input via `dispatchCommit`. Feedback hold 1000ms then acknowledgeFeedback. Lazy-loaded.\n- `app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx` — added `mode` state (radio segmented control), `clips` state from listClips(), `clipSupported` cached. `clipModeBlocked` disables Start when Clip selected + no tagged clips or rvfc absent. Start dispatches to `useClipRunner.start` vs `useSession.start`. Two new banners: `clip-mode-unsupported` + `clip-mode-no-clips`.\n- `app/src/ui/SummaryScreen.tsx` — added `mode` + `onClose` props. When `mode === 'clip'`, reads reps + config + inputSource from `useClipRunner`. Renders per-clip breakdown tables (`data-testid='per-clip-breakdown'`, `data-clip-id={clipId}`) for each unique clipId in the rep set.\n- `app/src/App.tsx` — clip-runner routing: when `clipPhase !== 'idle' && !== 'ended'` → ClipDrillScreen; when `clipPhase === 'ended'` → SummaryScreen mode='clip' onClose=resetClip+setView('idle'). Checked BEFORE live-session routing so a running clip drill is not pre-empted.\n- `app/src/App.css` — added `.mode-segmented` radio styles, `.visually-hidden` utility, `.clip-drill-stage` + `.clip-drill-video`, `.cue-table.per-clip` caption styling.\n- `app/verify-phase6-3.mjs` — NEW Playwright gate script: C1 mode-segmented control with Live default, C2 clip-mode-no-clips banner + Start disabled, C3 rvfc present on chromium (no unsupported banner), C4 seeded tagged clip → Start → ClipDrillScreen + video element mounted. All four PASS, console_errors=0.\n\nVerification:\n- 265/265 vitest tests pass (was 238; +27 new: 7 persistence + 2 runtime + 6 random + 12 runner).\n- Lint clean, tsc --noEmit clean.\n- Build clean. Bundle: main 356.10 KB / 109.40 KB gzip (was 346.98 / 107.30 in 6.2) → +9.12 KB raw / +2.10 KB gzip. New ClipDrillScreen chunk: 3.42 KB / 1.48 KB gzip. CSS: 14.67 / 3.47 KB (+0.83 / +0.19). Total clip-mode delta ≈ +5.0 KB gzip; budget +6 KB. Under.\n- verify-phase6-3.mjs C1/C2/C3/C4 all PASS, console_errors: 0.\n\nThings I'd like you to look hard at:\n1. The persistence.ts extraction — does it cover the DRY-gate invariant the red-team flagged (decision-memo concern 1)? Specifically: are both call sites (session.ts and clipmode/runner.ts) actually using it for ALL rep-shape decisions, or did I leak any inline logic?\n2. The clipmode/runner.ts rep-commit path: I bypass useSession for clip mode but use the same engine/persistence.commitRep + saveSession path. Did I miss any session-level state (e.g. roundIndex defaulting to 0 — is that wrong for clip mode? penaltyCounterEnabled = false hardcoded — OK?).\n3. The ClipDrillScreen rvfc loop: it re-arms itself in the callback. Is the cleanup function correct? Specifically: if `phase` changes from 'precue' to 'showing' mid-callback, does the next callback fire and potentially override markCueShown? Look at the cancelled flag semantics.\n4. The blob URL lifecycle in ClipDrillScreen.tsx: on currentClip change, URL.createObjectURL + assign to video.src + play(). The video element is the SAME element across clip changes. Is there a churn issue analogous to Phase 6.2's B2 (where setClip(updated) re-fired the effect)? Specifically: does the `currentClip` reference change every time `selectNextClip` runs even when the new clip is the same record from `pool`? It calls `pool.find(c => c.id === nextId)` — same reference.\n5. IdleScreen.tsx — does the `isClipModeSupported()` call inside `useState(() => ...)` initializer run on every re-render or once? (React docs: lazy initializer runs once.) And: is it correct to NOT re-check on subsequent renders, given that browser support doesn't change at runtime?\n6. Test coverage: I added 27 new tests. The clipmode/runner.test.ts uses the real Dexie (via fake-indexeddb). Is there any state-leak risk between tests, especially because the test uses `await flush(); await flush();` to wait for the fire-and-forget save?\n7. SummaryScreen.tsx now selects from BOTH useSession AND useClipRunner unconditionally (then picks based on the `mode` prop). Is the perf hit OK, or should this be branch-on-the-prop to avoid subscribing to two stores?\n8. The decision-memo §\"Project-complete signal\" says 6.3 approval should set `project_complete: true`. The wrapper writes `artifacts/project-complete.json` in a NEXT iteration. Confirm I should set this flag in phase-approval.json directly.\n\nReturn APPROVE / REQUEST_CHANGES with concrete findings (blocker / should-fix / nit), and file:line citations where applicable."}
