[tool_use] Write {"file_path":"/home/aaron/dev/projects/aaron/pointfight-reactor/artifacts/phase-approval.json","content":"{\n  \"phase\": \"phase-6.3\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"project_complete\": true,\n  \"summary\": \"Phase 6.3: clip-mode drill + RT measurement + per-clip results. The final phase of the Video Opponent Mode decomposition (Phase 6.1 storage → 6.2 tagging → 6.3 drill). Engine, store, and UI changes that wire clip playback through the same rep-scoring pipeline the live drill has used since Phase 1. New shared module `app/src/engine/persistence.ts` (`commitRep`, `mintSessionId`, `buildSessionRecord`, `persistSessionRecord`) is the single source of truth for rep-shape minting AND session-record persistence — both `store/session.ts` (live) and `clipmode/runner.ts` (clip) route through it (closes decision-memo Concern 1 + code-reviewer B3). `RepRecord` gains optional `clipId`; `SessionRecord` gains optional `mode: 'live'|'clip'` (undefined ≡ 'live' for back-compat). New `clipmode/runtime.ts:isClipModeSupported()` feature-detects `requestVideoFrameCallback` (Chrome 83+, Edge, Safari 15.4+) per §B5 measurement-coherence gate. New `clipmode/random.ts:pickNextClip()` implements uniform random with no-immediate-repeat, with 200-draw distribution test (each of 5 clips appears 32–48 times under seed 1) and 100-draw no-consecutive-duplicates test. New `clipmode/runner.ts` Zustand slice runs the drill state machine (idle → precue → showing → feedback → ended); `start()` filters to tagged clips via `selectTaggedClips`, `selectNextClip` bumps a `playSeq` counter on each call so the screen's rewind+play effect re-fires on single-clip pools (closes code-reviewer B1/B2), `recordPress` routes through `engine/persistence.commitRep` with the `clipId`, `stop()` persists with `mode: 'clip'`. New `app/src/ui/ClipDrillScreen.tsx` (lazy chunk: 3.54 KB / 1.51 KB gzip) mounts `<video>`, runs a separate rvfc loop watching `metadata.mediaTime * 1000 >= clip.cueAtMs` then calls `markCueShown(performance.now())`, splits blob-URL effect (keyed on `currentClip?.id`) from the rewind+play effect (keyed on `playSeq`) — same React-effect-churn shape Phase 6.2's B2 caught, but inverted. Keyboard + phone-peer input share the same `dispatchCommit` callback the TrainerScreen uses. `IdleScreen` gains a radio segmented control (`data-testid='mode-segmented'` with `mode-live` + `mode-clip`), two new banners (`clip-mode-unsupported` + `clip-mode-no-clips`), and a mode-dispatched Start that calls either `useSession.start` or `useClipRunner.start`. Clip-mode Start inherits the existing phone-pairing gate. `SummaryScreen` now accepts `mode` + `onClose` props; in clip mode it reads from `useClipRunner` and renders a per-clip breakdown (`data-testid='per-clip-breakdown'`, `data-clip-id=...`) for each unique clipId in the rep set, using `cueBreakdown(filteredReps)` so the Phase-5 analytics layer continues to work unchanged. `App.tsx` clip-runner routing precedes live-session routing so a running clip drill is not pre-empted by `useSession.phase==='idle'`. New `verify-phase6-3.mjs` C1–C4 gate checks (segmented control + live default, no-tagged-clips banner + Start disabled, rvfc present on chromium, seeded tagged clip → Start → ClipDrillScreen + video mounted). All four PASS with 0 console errors. M1–M6 manual checklist enumerates real-device QA per §B5 (±33 ms cue-shown precision against real `<video>` + real .mp4). 33 new vitest tests (271 total, was 238; +7 persistence + 2 runtime + 6 random + 16 runner [12 original + 4 regression/wire tests] + 2 session wire tests). Lint + tsc + vite build all clean. Main bundle 356.23 KB / 109.46 KB gzip (Phase 6.2 baseline 346.98 / 107.30 — delta +9.25 KB raw / +2.16 KB gzip); ClipDrillScreen chunk 3.54 / 1.51 KB gzip; CSS chunk +0.83 KB raw / +0.19 KB gzip. Total clip-mode delta ≈ +5.2 KB gzip; budget was +6 KB. Under budget. Code-reviewer (`code-reviewer` agent) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with 4 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits; all blockers + 3 of 5 should-fixes applied before this approval: (B1) `ClipDrillScreen` blob-URL effect split from a separate rewind+play effect keyed on `playSeq`; single-clip pool rep 2+ now rewinds and replays the video on every `selectNextClip` — regression test 'bumps playSeq on every selectNextClip, including back-to-back single-clip pool' added to runner.test.ts; (B2) collapses into B1 — once the video rewinds, the rvfc loop fires `markCueShown` only after `mediaTime * 1000 >= cueAtMs` on the fresh playback, not immediately on the stale paused frame; (B3) `persistSession` closures in `session.ts` + `runner.ts` collapsed into shared `engine/persistence.buildSessionRecord` + `persistSessionRecord`; both stores now route session persistence through one function — regression test 'routes session persistence through engine/persistence.persistSessionRecord' wires this both ways via `vi.spyOn`; (B4) wire-tests added asserting both `useSession.recordPress` and `useClipRunner.recordPress` call `engine/persistence.commitRep` (would fail if either call site reverted to inline rep-minting); (S1) `newId()` and `newSessionId()` collapsed into shared `engine/persistence.mintSessionId()`; (S4) `selectNextClip` now guards `phase !== 'idle' && phase !== 'feedback' → return`, preventing future foot-guns where a precue/showing call would clobber an in-flight rep — regression test 'selectNextClip is a no-op when called from precue or showing' added; (S5) inline comments now explain why `roundIndex: 0` / `cleared: 0` / `penaltyCounterEnabled: false` are hardcoded in clip mode. Should-fixes S2 (phaseRef stale-read race) is defense-in-depth — slice-level guards catch it, so explicitly documented as not blocking. S3 (prototype mutation across parallel tests) is fine under vitest's worker-per-file model. Nits N1–N4 (glyph choice, flush() comment cleanup, banner waitForSelector race, IdleScreen.test.tsx coverage) — N1/N2/N3 left as-is per reviewer note that they are not blocking; N4 (an IdleScreen.test.tsx for the segmented control) is intentionally NOT added because the three-layer test architecture introduced in Phase 6.2's decision-memo locks the segmented-control UI to verify-phaseN.mjs gates (C1/C2/C3 all PASS) — adding a fourth assertion path would duplicate what verify-phase6-3.mjs already gates. Phase 6.3 closes the Video Opponent Mode acceptance criteria; Phase 7 (Webcam Pose Detection) is post-tournament and explicitly deferred per `docs/SPEC.md` §'Non-Goals for MVP' (`'Perfect pose detection'`). The wrapper's next iteration writes `artifacts/project-complete.json` with `final_phase: '6.3'` and `deferred: ['phase-7']` per `artifacts/decision-memo.md` §'Project-complete signal at 6.3'.\",\n  \"decision_memo\": \"artifacts/decision-memo.md\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"engine/persistence.ts exposes commitRep(...) containing the invariants currently inlined in session.ts:107-139. Both session.ts and clipmode/runner.ts call it.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/engine/persistence.ts:60-83` defines `commitRep(input): CommitRepResult` covering rep-id minting (`newRepId`), `resolveCueAtDistance`, the `roundIndex` + `inputSource` fan-out, optional `distance` and `clipId` spread, and `saveRep` side-effect. `app/src/store/session.ts:97-117` calls into it; `app/src/clipmode/runner.ts:127-144` calls into it with `clipId`. Wire-tests in `session.test.ts` ('routes recordPress through engine/persistence.commitRep') and `runner.test.ts` ('routes recordPress through engine/persistence.commitRep') both use `vi.spyOn(persistence, 'commitRep')` and assert it is called exactly once — would fail if either call site reverted to inline rep-minting (closes code-reviewer B4). `persistence.test.ts` covers the rep shape across 7 tests including distance omission/inclusion + clipId omission/inclusion + id uniqueness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"RepRecord gains clipId?: string. SessionRecord gains mode?: 'live'|'clip' (undefined ≡ 'live' for back-compat).\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/engine/types.ts:51-58` adds `clipId?: string` to RepRecord with a comment explaining it's set only for clip-mode reps and back-compat is preserved by the field being optional. Lines 78-90 add `mode?: 'live' | 'clip'` to SessionRecord with a comment that `undefined` is treated as `'live'`. The schema additions are validated by `persistence.test.ts` 'writes the clipId field when set' (sets clipId, asserts rep.clipId equals it) and 'omits the clipId field when undefined' (asserts `'clipId' in rep === false`). Session-record `mode` field is exercised by `runner.test.ts` 'stop() persists the session with mode=\\\"clip\\\"' and 'acknowledgeFeedback at maxReps ends the session and persists with mode=\\\"clip\\\"'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"clipmode/runner.ts selects clips by uniform random with replacement, no repeat-immediately-previous. Untagged excluded. 200-draw distribution test: each of 5 clips appears 32–48 times. 100-draw no-repeat-prev test: no consecutive duplicates.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/clipmode/random.ts:24-46` `pickNextClip(rng, ids, previousId)` filters out `previousId` from the candidate pool when the pool size ≥ 2. `random.test.ts` covers all six branches: empty (throws), single-clip (returns it regardless of prev), two-clip no-repeat (50 iterations all non-repeat), 100-draw no-consecutive-duplicates, 200-draw distribution under mulberry32(1) (asserts each of {a,b,c,d,e} lands in [32, 48]), and prev-not-in-list fallback. `runner.ts:38-40` `selectTaggedClips()` filters on `cueId !== undefined && cueAtMs !== undefined`; `runner.test.ts` 'selectTaggedClips keeps clips with both cueId and cueAtMs set' covers the predicate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"IdleScreen adds a segmented control above Start with data-testid='mode-segmented' exposing mode-live + mode-clip options. Default live. Start dispatches based on mode; no second Start button. Clip-mode Start inherits phone-pairing gate.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/ui/IdleScreen.tsx:131-159` renders a `<fieldset data-testid='mode-segmented'>` with two radio inputs (`mode-live` checked by default, `mode-clip`). `handleStart` at line 76-86 dispatches to `useClipRunner.start(clips, profile.config, undefined, settings.inputSource)` when mode is 'clip', else `useSession.start`. There is only one Start button (line 161-168). The `phoneSelected && !phoneReady` gate at line 73 is part of `startDisabled`, applying to both modes. verify-phase6-3.mjs C1 PASS asserts the segmented control + both options + live-default-checked; C4 PASS confirms Start dispatches into ClipDrillScreen when Clip is selected with a tagged clip present.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"clipmode/runtime.ts:isClipModeSupported() returns false when requestVideoFrameCallback is absent. IdleScreen renders data-testid='clip-mode-unsupported' banner and disables Start.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/clipmode/runtime.ts:13-17` checks `'requestVideoFrameCallback' in HTMLVideoElement.prototype`. `runtime.test.ts` covers both branches (present + absent) by mutating the prototype via `Object.defineProperty`. `IdleScreen.tsx:39` caches the result via `useState(() => isClipModeSupported())` (lazy initializer — runs once, since browser support doesn't change at runtime). `IdleScreen.tsx:97-105` renders the `clip-mode-unsupported` banner when `mode === 'clip' && !clipSupported`. `clipModeBlocked` at line 67-68 disables Start in that case. verify-phase6-3.mjs C3 PASS confirms the unsupported banner is NOT shown under headless chromium (which uniformly ships rvfc); the false-branch path is covered by `runtime.test.ts` 'returns false when requestVideoFrameCallback is missing'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Selecting Clip mode with zero tagged clips disables Start with a data-testid='clip-mode-no-clips' banner pointing to the library.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`IdleScreen.tsx:107-126` renders the `clip-mode-no-clips` banner when `mode === 'clip' && clipSupported && taggedClips.length === 0`, with a button calling `onOpenClips` to navigate to the library. `clipModeBlocked` at line 67-68 is true when `taggedClips.length === 0` in clip mode, disabling Start. verify-phase6-3.mjs C2 PASS asserts banner is present + Start is disabled when no tagged clips exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"ClipDrillScreen.tsx mounts <video>, drives the runner, renders the same feedback UI as TrainerScreen. cueShownAt = clipStartedAt + clip.cueAtMs computed via requestVideoFrameCallback callback timestamp.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/ui/ClipDrillScreen.tsx:175-184` renders `<video ref={videoRef} data-testid='clip-drill-video' onPlaying={() => markClipStarted(performance.now())}>`. The rvfc loop at lines 126-150 polls `metadata.mediaTime * 1000 >= clip.cueAtMs` and calls `markCueShown(performance.now())` on the first crossing. Feedback rendering at lines 202-211 mirrors TrainerScreen's structure (same `.feedback`, `.feedback-label`, `.feedback-sub` classes and the same `feedbackLabel(result)` switch). The ±33 ms precision criterion is gated by manual QA M3 per §B5 (real `<video>` + rvfc against a clip on disk); headless chromium with synthesized blobs does not validate this end-to-end. The split blob-URL / rewind-and-play effects close code-reviewer B1 + B2 — regression test 'bumps playSeq on every selectNextClip' in runner.test.ts catches the single-clip-pool repeat case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Saved SessionRecord.mode === 'clip'; each RepRecord has the correct clipId. Phase-5 analytics (cueBreakdown, antiRhythmSignal, best10AvgOf) continue to work unchanged on the additive fields.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`runner.test.ts` 'stop() persists the session with mode=\\\"clip\\\" and endedAt set' reads back from Dexie and asserts `stored?.mode === 'clip'`. 'recordPress within hesitation threshold on a go cue → correct_go with clipId' asserts `rep.clipId === 'alpha'`. 'recordPress before cue (during precue) records a false_start with clipId' and 'finishWindow with no press on a go cue records late with clipId' cover the false_start + late branches. Phase-5 analytics unchanged: `cueBreakdown`, `antiRhythmSignal`, `best10AvgOf`, `correctGoTimesOf` all consume `RepRecord[]` and are unchanged; existing 26 analytics tests still pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"SummaryScreen shows a per-clip breakdown when mode === 'clip', using cueBreakdown(reps) filtered by clipId.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"`app/src/ui/SummaryScreen.tsx:48-65` builds `perClipBreakdown` by grouping `reps` by `clipId`, then calling `cueBreakdown(filteredReps)` per group, attaching the clip name from `clipPool`. The render block at lines 121-159 emits one `<table data-testid='per-clip-breakdown' data-clip-id={clipId}>` per unique clipId. The Phase-5 `cueBreakdown` function is reused unchanged — same source-of-truth for cue/RT/score columns. The cross-mode prop API (`mode='live'` default + `mode='clip'` branch) is exercised via the App.tsx routing: `clipPhase === 'ended' → SummaryScreen mode='clip'`.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Lint + tsc + vitest + vite build clean. Bundle growth budget: +6 KB gzip for runner + drill screen + persistence helper.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"All four are clean. 271/271 vitest tests pass (Phase 6.2 baseline 238; +33 new). Bundle: main 356.23 KB / 109.46 KB gzip (Phase 6.2 baseline 346.98 / 107.30 → delta +9.25 KB raw / +2.16 KB gzip). New ClipDrillScreen chunk: 3.54 KB / 1.51 KB gzip. CSS: 14.67 / 3.47 KB gzip (+0.83 raw / +0.19 gzip). Total clip-mode delta ≈ +5.2 KB gzip — under the +6 KB gzip budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"Manual real-device QA at app/verify-phase6-3.mjs. The ±33 ms cue-shown precision criterion is MANUAL per §B5.\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"verify-phase6-3.mjs writes the M1–M6 manual_qa_checklist to results.json: M1 (tag a real .mp4 clip with cueId='blitzes' + cueAtMs≈1500), M2 (Start Clip mode; clip auto-plays; WATCH overlay), M3 (press commit after cue; reactionMs lands within ~33 ms of tagged frame), M4 (Stop drill; SummaryScreen per-clip breakdown), M5 (Manage clips: tagged clip unchanged — clip-mode does not mutate the clip record), M6 (SessionRecord.mode === 'clip' + RepRecord.clipId per Dexie inspection). Automated run: C1 PASS + C2 PASS + C3 PASS + C4 PASS, console_errors=0. Per `QUALITY_GATES.md` §'Browser-API limitations (Phase 2b + Phase 6)' §B5, real `<video>` + real `requestVideoFrameCallback` against a real .mp4 file is the MANUAL gate; headless chromium decoding of synthesized blobs is unreliable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"criterion\": \"The 6.3 phase-approval.json sets project_complete: true at the top level; the next iteration writes artifacts/project-complete.json with final_phase: '6.3' and deferred: ['phase-7'].\",\n      \"verified_by\": \"This artifact has `\\\"project_complete\\\": true` at top level (line 4). Per `artifacts/decision-memo.md` §'Project-complete signal at 6.3' the wrapper's next iteration writes `artifacts/project-complete.json` with `{ \\\"complete\\\": true, \\\"final_phase\\\": \\\"6.3\\\", \\\"deferred\\\": [\\\"phase-7\\\"], \\\"deferred_reason\\\": \\\"post-tournament; not required for MVP per docs/SPEC.md\\\" }`. Phase 7 (Webcam Pose Detection) is explicitly post-tournament per `docs/SPEC.md` §'Non-Goals for MVP' ('Perfect pose detection') and `docs/PHASES.md:312-315` ('Phase 7: Webcam Pose Detection Prototype [post-tournament]').\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manual_qa\": {\n    \"device_used\": \"not_performed_by_agent\",\n    \"performed_by\": \"autonomous-agent\",\n    \"performed_at\": \"2026-05-27\",\n    \"playwright_run\": {\n      \"automated_gate_checks\": \"C1, C2, C3, C4 PASS — IdleScreen renders mode-segmented control with Live default; selecting Clip with no tagged clips shows the no-clips banner + disables Start; rvfc is present on chromium so the unsupported banner is not shown; a seeded tagged clip + Start transitions into ClipDrillScreen with the <video> element mounted. Zero console errors across all four contexts.\",\n      \"console_errors\": 0\n    },\n    \"checklist_pending_operator_sign_off\": [\n      \"M1 — Tag a real .mp4 clip (cueId='blitzes', cueAtMs ≈ 1500).\",\n      \"M2 — Start Clip mode. Clip auto-plays; WATCH overlay visible until cueAtMs.\",\n      \"M3 — Press commit just after cue. Feedback shows reactionMs within ±33 ms of the tagged frame.\",\n      \"M4 — Stop the drill. SummaryScreen shows per-clip breakdown.\",\n      \"M5 — Re-open Manage clips: tagged clip unchanged.\",\n      \"M6 — SessionRecord.mode === 'clip'; each RepRecord carries the correct clipId (DevTools inspection).\"\n    ],\n    \"operator_sign_off_instructions\": \"Update artifacts/phase-6-3-verify/results.json — set each entry's `signed_off` to {date: 'YYYY-MM-DD', device: '<laptop OS + browser version>'} after exercising the step on a real laptop with a real .mp4 file. The §B5 concession requires this field to be populated before the phase is considered fully closed for real-world use; the autonomous loop cannot perform real-video + rvfc + ±33 ms cue-shown precision QA. M3 in particular requires the operator to eyeball-check whether the reactionMs reported matches the tagged frame within one frame (~33 ms at 30 fps); M6 requires DevTools inspection of the Dexie sessions/reps tables. M1+M2+M3 prove the play → cue → press primary loop; M4 proves the per-clip summary; M5 proves clip-mode does not mutate the clip record; M6 proves the new schema fields are written correctly.\"\n  },\n  \"gates\": {\n    \"testing\": \"271/271 vitest tests pass (Phase 6.2 baseline 238; +33 new). Every new public behavior has a would-fail-if-reverted test: `engine/persistence.commitRep` (rep shape + persistence + clipId optionality + id uniqueness, 7 tests); `engine/persistence.buildSessionRecord` + `persistSessionRecord` (via session/runner wire tests); `clipmode/runtime.isClipModeSupported` (both branches, 2 tests); `clipmode/random.pickNextClip` (200-draw distribution + 100-draw no-repeat-prev + 4 edge cases, 6 tests); `clipmode/runner` (state machine + persistence round-trip + inputSource fan-out + false_start/late branches with clipId + maxReps end + B1/B3/B4/S4 regressions, 16 tests). The wire tests in `session.test.ts` and `runner.test.ts` spy on `persistence.commitRep` and `persistence.persistSessionRecord` via `vi.spyOn`, asserting both call sites delegate — the DRY-gate guarantee the decision-memo Concern 1 required (closes code-reviewer B4).\",\n    \"dry\": \"engine/persistence.ts is now the single source of truth for: rep-id minting (`newRepId`), session-id minting (`mintSessionId`), rep building + persistence (`commitRep`), session-record building (`buildSessionRecord`), and session-record persistence with error hand-off (`persistSessionRecord`). Both `store/session.ts` and `clipmode/runner.ts` route through these helpers exclusively — no inline rep or session record construction remains in either store. The wire tests would fail if either call site reverted to inline minting. `clipmode/random.ts:pickNextClip` is the single source for clip selection. `clipmode/runtime.ts:isClipModeSupported` is the single source for the rvfc feature detection. `Phase-5` analytics (`cueBreakdown`, `antiRhythmSignal`, `best10AvgOf`, `correctGoTimesOf`, `summarize`) are reused unchanged — clip-mode adds no parallel implementation.\",\n    \"drift\": \"No prior-phase invariants touched. Phase 6.1 Dexie v4 schema unchanged. Phase 6.2 ClipRecord shape (cueId/cueAtMs as optional fields written by `updateClipTag`) is consumed unchanged here. Phase-5 analytics unchanged. Phase 2b.4 phone-input subscription pattern reused in ClipDrillScreen via the same `dispatchCommit` callback shape TrainerScreen uses. `IdleScreen` gains the segmented control + two new banners but the existing keyboard/pedal/phone start path is unchanged (preserved by the `mode === 'live'` branch). `SummaryScreen` gains optional props with `'live'` default so all existing call sites (App.tsx's `phase === 'ended'` route) continue to render the live-mode summary unchanged.\",\n    \"planning\": \"Phase 6 was decomposed in a prior iteration via strategy-planner + architecture-red-team round-trip, recorded in artifacts/decision-memo.md §'Phase 6 decomposition memo' through §'Resolved red-team blockers — Phase 6' (including §B5 browser-API limitations + §B6 falsifiable acceptance + Concern 1 DRY extraction + Concern 5 rvfc gate + Concern 7 random distribution + Concern 10 project-complete signal). Phase 6.3 acceptance criteria in docs/PHASES.md were the locked-in source of truth for this iteration; no new planner invocation needed. Architecture-red-team not re-invoked — no new architectural surface (the engine/persistence extraction, rvfc gate, no-repeat-prev distribution, single segmented control, and project-complete signal were all settled in the original Phase 6 decomposition).\",\n    \"verification_sprint\": \"Pre-phase: 238/238 vitest tests + lint + tsc + vite build at the Phase 6.2 boundary all clean (re-confirmed at the top of this iteration). Post-phase: 271/271 + lint + tsc + build all clean. Verify-phase6-3.mjs C1–C4 PASS, 0 console errors. The full live-drill flow (Phase 1-5 + 2b.1-4) is regression-covered by the 218 pre-Phase-6.3 tests that remain green.\",\n    \"pre_commit_verify\": \"scripts/phasekit-verify.sh runs lint + typecheck + tests; all pass.\"\n  },\n  \"review\": {\n    \"architecture_red_team\": \"Cross-cutting Phase-6 concerns (§B5 browser-API limitations + §B6 falsifiable acceptance) unchanged in this phase — both were locked in during the prior decomposition iteration and are observed here (manual_qa block + every acceptance criterion is AUTO+GATE or MANUAL with explicit rationale). Concern 5 (Safari < 15.4 rvfc absence → measurement incoherence) is gated by isClipModeSupported() + the data-testid='clip-mode-unsupported' banner — the same shape as Phase 2b's phone-pairing gate. Concern 1 (DRY extraction) is satisfied by the engine/persistence module + wire-tests. No new architectural risks introduced.\",\n    \"code_reviewer\": \"REQUEST_CHANGES with 4 blockers + 5 should-fix + 4 nits. All blockers + 3 of 5 should-fixes APPLIED before approval: (B1) ClipDrillScreen blob-URL effect split from a separate rewind+play effect keyed on `playSeq`; single-clip pool rep 2+ now correctly rewinds + replays — regression test 'bumps playSeq on every selectNextClip, including back-to-back single-clip pool' added; (B2) collapses into B1 — once the video rewinds, the rvfc loop fires `markCueShown` only after the fresh playback crosses `cueAtMs`; (B3) `persistSession` closures in session.ts + runner.ts collapsed into shared `engine/persistence.buildSessionRecord` + `persistSessionRecord` — regression test 'routes session persistence through engine/persistence.persistSessionRecord' wires this; (B4) wire-tests added asserting both `useSession.recordPress` and `useClipRunner.recordPress` route through `engine/persistence.commitRep` via `vi.spyOn` — would fail if either call site reverted to inline rep-minting; (S1) `newId()` + `newSessionId()` collapsed into shared `engine/persistence.mintSessionId()`; (S4) `selectNextClip` guard tightened to no-op outside `idle`/`feedback` — regression test added; (S5) inline comments added explaining clip-mode hardcoded zeros for roundIndex/cleared/penaltyCounterEnabled. Should-fixes S2 + S3 noted as defense-in-depth and not blocking by the reviewer; not applied. Nits N1-N4 left as-is per reviewer non-blocking note. The project-complete signal at line 4 of this artifact is confirmed by the reviewer against decision-memo §Concern-10.\",\n    \"qa_playwright\": \"Phase 6.3 user-visible surface is gated by automated checks C1–C4 in verify-phase6-3.mjs (all PASS) plus the M1–M6 manual checklist under §B5. Real `<video>` + `requestVideoFrameCallback` + ±33 ms cue-shown precision against a real .mp4 file cannot be exercised under headless chromium (synthesized blobs do not decode reliably to a measurable cue moment); manual operator sign-off is the authoritative gate for those paths per the decision memo §B5 concession. Phase 6.2 + Phase 6.1 + Phase 5 + Phase 2b regression: not separately re-run this iteration; covered by the full vitest suite (271/271) which gates the library + clip-library + analytics + drill + profiles + WebRTC pairing + motion + InputSource modules unchanged in this phase.\"\n  },\n  \"suggested_commit_message\": \"phase-6.3: clip-mode drill + engine/persistence extraction + per-clip summary\"\n}\n"}
